  "how_to_tell_apart": "Danish and Bokmål share jeg, ikke, og, et and skal, so those are poor separators. Lean on af versus Norwegian av, noget versus noe, hedder versus heter, and the capital I / jer for ‘you (plural)’, which Swedish would render as ni and Bokmål as dere. Against Swedish, the vowels æ and ø plus og/er/ikke are the quick orthographic test; against Nynorsk, Danish will not show eg, ikkje, eit, kva or korleis.",
